refentry.refsect1:
&reftitle.description;
arrayfalsestream_socket_pair intdomain inttype intprotocol
stream_socket_pair creates a pair of connected, indistinguishable socket streams. This function is commonly used in IPC (Inter-Process Communication).

&reftitle.returnvalues;


 Returns an array with the two socket resources on success, or
 &false; on failure.

  &reftitle.examples;



    A stream_socket_pair example


     This example shows that what is written to one socket of the pair is read
     from the other one. The same pair is commonly used between two processes,
     for example after pcntl_fork.



<?php

$sockets = stream_socket_pair(STREAM_PF_UNIX, STREAM_SOCK_STREAM, STREAM_IPPROTO_IP);

fwrite($sockets[0], "message from the first socket\n");
echo fgets($sockets[1]);

fwrite($sockets[1], "reply from the second socket\n");
echo fgets($sockets[0]);

fclose($sockets[0]);
fclose($sockets[1]);


    &example.outputs;


message from the first socket
reply from the second socket
